rapt (0.1.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The apt repository is laid out per suite rather than flat, so a client
    is only ever offered builds for its own release.
  * Binary packages are built for every suite and architecture r2u serves.

 -- Troy Hernandez <troy@cornball.ai>  Tue, 11 Aug 2026 16:05:00 +0000

rapt (0.1.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The /etc/R/profile.d/rapt.R drop-in is quiet by default. Set
    RAPT_VERBOSE=TRUE to restore the startup message.
  * enable() and disable() gained a verbose argument, defaulting to
    option rapt.verbose.
  * Drop-ins ending in .r are sourced alongside .R.

 -- Troy Hernandez <troy@cornball.ai>  Mon, 10 Aug 2026 12:18:45 +0000

